{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses: Send forth your hand and seize it by its tail.</b> The tail signifies the utmost lowliness, and He hinted to him that upon their lowliness — for they were already lowly as crawlers of the dust — there would be added yet further lowliness, like the tail of the serpent which is lower than all the rest of the body; so too would their lowliness increase, as indeed happened to them when it was said: ״תִּכְבַּד הָעֲבוֹדָה עַל הָאֲנָשִׁים״ (Exodus 5:9), in that they were not given straw. And from that lowest rung, in the uttermost depth of lowliness, from there they would ascend and return to their former eminence, to become like this upright staff. And this matter was hinted to Moses in what was said to him: ״אֱחֹז בִּזְנָבוֹ״, ״וַיִּשְׁלַח יָדוֹ וַיַּחֲזֶק בּוֹ וַיְהִי לְמַטֶּה בְּכַפּוֹ״ (Exodus 4:4) — and it is a very fitting allusion to what would ultimately happen to them, for ״מַגִּיד מֵרֵאשִׁית אַחֲרִית״ (Isaiah 46:10): He disclosed to his ear that they would become like the tail of the serpent, that is, an addition of lowliness upon their lowliness, and from there they would ascend to become a ruling staff that subdues Pharaoh and all his people. And in this the Holy One, blessed be He, gave him a sign that it is in His hand, blessed be He, to bring low and to lift up — ״מֵאַשְׁפֹּת אֶבְיוֹן״ (Psalms 113:7). And in the proximate passage of Va'era (Exodus 7:9), with the help of HaShem, the matter of the serpent will be explained in a different respect; see there."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:20.703330567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}